perator-level data about what actually works for $500 solo founders in Vietnam. This is the research itself telling us something: the conventional knowledge sources (articles, reports, market analyses) are structurally unable to answer this question because they study COMPANIES and MARKETS, not OPERATORS. The real intelligence sits in Vietnamese forums (mmo4me, voz.vn), Telegram/Zalo groups of actual operators, and reverse-engineering visible success cases. The analytical framework is sound but the INPUT DATA is wrong — it's corporate-lens data applied to a street-level question. Any model recommendation based purely on this research would be narrative-fitting, not evidence-based.\"}"
